{"step_index":137,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:58:53Z","thinking":"**Evaluating the roman_domination_number statement**\n\nConsidering the statement: (nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number. The challenge is labeled 'open' which suggests its difficulty. The goal is to prove this statement or find a counterexample.\n\n\n**Formulating the Lean 4 proof**\n\nThe Lean 4 `Candidate` statement precisely captures the conjecture. Definitions of `IsNontrivialClass`, `order`, `ballWithin`, `eccentricity`, and `radius` are now available within `GraphCalc`. It appears we need to translate the informal proof into a formal Lean 4 structure.\n\n\n**Analyzing the lower bound of radius**\n\n`radius G` is the minimum eccentricity. The definition of `romanDominationNumber G` involves the weights of all valid Roman dominating functions. To show `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`, for all valid $f$, requires examining individual function weights. The approach needs to link graph radius with the function's weight.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nfrom itertools import product\n\n# For small graphs, test ALL Roman dominating functions f\n# Check if exists v in V with ecc(v) + 1 <= weight(f)\nfound_violation = False\nfor n in range(2, 7):\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n        if G.number_of_nodes() == n and nx.is_connected(G):\n            nodes = list(G.nodes())\n            eccs = {v: nx.eccentricity(G, v) for v in nodes}\n            min_ecc = min(eccs.values())\n            for f_tup in product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n                valid = True\n                for i, v in enumerate(nodes):\n                    if f_tup[i] == 0:\n                        if not any(f_tup[nodes.index(u)] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)):\n                            valid = False\n                            break\n                if valid:\n                    w = sum(f_tup)\n                    # Does min_ecc + 1 <= w?\n                    if min_ecc + 1 > w:\n                        print(f'VIOLATION: n={n}, min_ecc={min_ecc}, w={w}')\n                        found_violation = True\n                        break\n            if found_violation:\n                break\n    if found_violation:\n        break\n\nif not found_violation:\n    print('For ALL Roman dominating functions on all connected graphs up to n=6, min_ecc + 1 <= weight(f) HOLDS!')\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":15000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Check if min_ecc + 1 <= weight(f) for ALL RDFs"}}]}
