{"step_index":152,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:59:23Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T16:59:23+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T16:59:25+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/LeanProject/GraphInvariants.lean`\nTotal Lines: 222\nTotal Bytes: 11395\nShowing lines 1 to 200\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: /-\n2: GraphInvariants.lean — a small, faithful Lean 4 / mathlib formalization layer for\n3: the graph invariants that appear in the *simplest* CEGIS survivors, so that the\n4: machine-generated conjectures are well-formed `theorem … := sorry` goals the\n5: DeepSeek-Prover-V2 backend (and the kernel) can actually act on.\n6: \n7: Scope is deliberately small. Invariants already in mathlib are reused directly:\n8: \n9:   order n            → `Fintype.card V`        (aliased `SimpleGraph.order`)\n10:   size m             → `G.edgeFinset.card`     (aliased `SimpleGraph.size`)\n11:   minimum_degree δ   → `G.minDegree`           (mathlib)\n12:   maximum_degree Δ   → `G.maxDegree`           (mathlib)\n13:   clique_number ω    → `G.cliqueNum`           (mathlib)\n14:   independence_num α → `G.indepNum`            (mathlib)\n15:   chromatic_number χ → `G.chromaticNumber`     (mathlib, ℕ∞)\n16: \n17: Invariants *not* in mathlib but faithfully definable in a few lines are defined\n18: here (domination family). Harder invariants (zero forcing, residue, Roman\n19: domination, …) are intentionally out of scope: conjectures referencing them are\n20: filtered out of the prove set rather than formalized incorrectly.\n21: -/\n22: import Mathlib\n23: \n24: open scoped Classical\n25: \n26: namespace SimpleGraph\n27: \n28: variable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n29: \n30: /-- Order of `G`: the number of vertices. -/\n31: def order (_G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ := Fintype.card V\n32: \n33: /-- Size of `G`: the number of edges. -/\n34: noncomputable def size (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n35:   G.edgeFinset.card\n36: \n37: /-- `s` dominates `G`: every vertex is in `s` or adjacent to a vertex of `s`. -/\n38: def IsDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n39:   ∀ v : V, v ∈ s ∨ ∃ w ∈ s, G.Adj v w\n40: \n41: /-- Domination number `γ(G)`: minimum cardinality of a dominating set. -/\n42: noncomputable def dominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n43:   sInf { n | ∃ s : Finset V, s.card = n ∧ G.IsDominatingSet s }\n44: \n45: /-- `s` is independent in `G`: no two of its vertices are adjacent. -/\n46: def IsIndependentFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n47:   ∀ ⦃u⦄, u ∈ s → ∀ ⦃w⦄, w ∈ s → ¬ G.Adj u w\n48: \n49: /-- Independent domination number `i(G)`: minimum cardinality of an independent\n50: dominating set. -/\n51: noncomputable def independentDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n52:   sInf { n | ∃ s : Finset V, s.card = n ∧ G.IsDominatingSet s ∧ G.IsIndependentFinset s }\n53: \n54: /- ── Degree-sequence invariants ─────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n55: \n56: /-- Degrees in non-decreasing order. -/\n57: noncomputable def degreesAsc (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : List ℕ :=\n58:   (Finset.univ.val.map (fun v => G.degree v)).sort (· ≤ ·)\n59: \n60: /-- Degrees in non-increasing order. -/\n61: noncomputable def degreesDesc (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : List ℕ :=\n62:   (Finset.univ.val.map (fun v => G.degree v)).sort (· ≥ ·)\n63: \n64: /-- Annihilation number `a(G)`: the largest `k ≤ n` such that the `k` smallest\n65: degrees sum to at most the number of edges. -/\n66: noncomputable def annihilationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n67:   sSup { k | k ≤ Fintype.card V ∧ ((G.degreesAsc).take k).sum ≤ G.size }\n68: \n69: /-- Slater number `sl(G)`: the least `t` with `t + (sum of the t largest degrees) ≥ n`.\n70: A classical lower bound on the domination number. -/\n71: noncomputable def slaterNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n72:   sInf { t | (Fintype.card V) ≤ t + ((G.degreesDesc).take t).sum }\n73: \n74: /- ── Zero forcing family ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n75: \n76: /-- One zero-forcing colour-change step: a blue vertex with a unique white\n77: neighbour forces it blue. -/\n78: noncomputable def forcingStep (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n79:     (S : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n80:   S ∪ Finset.univ.filter (fun w => w ∉ S ∧ ∃ v ∈ S, G.neighborFinset v \\ S = {w})\n81: \n82: /-- Zero-forcing closure: iterate the step `|V|` times (a fixpoint is reached, as\n83: each non-final step adds at least one vertex). -/\n84: noncomputable def forcingClosure (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n85:     (S : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n86:   (G.forcingStep)^[Fintype.card V] S\n87: \n88: /-- `S` is a zero-forcing set if its closure is everything. -/\n89: def IsZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n90:   G.forcingClosure S = Finset.univ\n91: \n92: /-- Zero forcing number `Z(G)`: minimum size of a zero-forcing set. -/\n93: noncomputable def zeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n94:   sInf { k | ∃ S : Finset V, S.card = k ∧ G.IsZeroForcingSet S }\n95: \n96: /-- A total zero-forcing set: zero-forcing and inducing no isolated vertex. -/\n97: def IsTotalZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n98:   G.IsZeroForcingSet S ∧ ∀ v ∈ S, ∃ w ∈ S, G.Adj v w\n99: \n100: /-- Total zero forcing number `Z_t(G)`. -/\n101: noncomputable def totalZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n102:   sInf { k | ∃ S : Finset V, S.card = k ∧ G.IsTotalZeroForcingSet S }\n103: \n104: /-- A connected zero-forcing set: zero-forcing and inducing a connected subgraph. -/\n105: def IsConnectedZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n106:   G.IsZeroForcingSet S ∧ (G.induce (↑S)).Connected\n107: \n108: /-- Connected zero forcing number `Z_c(G)`. -/\n109: noncomputable def connectedZeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n110:   sInf { k | ∃ S : Finset V, S.card = k ∧ G.IsConnectedZeroForcingSet S }\n111: \n112: /-- `s` totally dominates `G`: every vertex has a neighbour in `s` (a vertex\n113: does not dominate itself). -/\n114: def IsTotalDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n115:   ∀ v : V, ∃ w ∈ s, G.Adj v w\n116: \n117: /-- Total domination number `γ_t(G)`. Undefined (here: `sInf ∅ = 0`) on a graph\n118: with an isolated vertex; the computable mirror carries an explicit definedness\n119: predicate, and the exporters emit it as a hypothesis. -/\n120: noncomputable def totalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n121:   sInf { n | ∃ s : Finset V, s.card = n ∧ G.IsTotalDominatingSet s }\n122: \n123: /-- `s` is an edge cover: every vertex lies on some edge of `s`. -/\n124: def IsEdgeCoverFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) (s : Finset (Sym2 V)) : Prop :=\n125:   ↑s ⊆ G.edgeSet ∧ ∀ v : V, ∃ e ∈ s, v ∈ e\n126: \n127: /-- Edge cover number `ρ(G)`: minimum size of an edge cover. Undefined on a\n128: graph with an isolated vertex. -/\n129: noncomputable def edgeCoverNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n130:   sInf { n | ∃ s : Finset (Sym2 V), s.card = n ∧ G.IsEdgeCoverFinset s }\n131: \n132: /-- Sub-total domination number: least `t` whose `t` largest degrees sum to at\n133: least `n` (Davila). -/\n134: noncomputable def subTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V)\n135:     [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n136:   sInf { t | Fintype.card V ≤ ((G.degreesDesc).take t).sum }\n137: \n138: /-- `f` is a Roman dominating function: every vertex labelled `0` has a\n139: neighbour labelled `2`. -/\n140: def IsRomanDominatingFunction (G : SimpleGraph V) (f : V → Fin 3) : Prop :=\n141:   ∀ v : V, f v = 0 → ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ f u = 2\n142: \n143: /-- Roman domination number `γ_R(G)`: minimum weight `Σ f v` over Roman\n144: dominating functions. -/\n145: noncomputable def romanDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ :=\n146:   sInf { n | ∃ f : V → Fin 3, G.IsRomanDominatingFunction f ∧ ∑ v, (f v : ℕ) = n }\n147: \n148: /-- `f` is a double Roman dominating function: a vertex labelled `0` has a\n149: neighbour labelled `3` or two neighbours labelled `2`, and a vertex labelled `1`\n150: has a neighbour labelled at least `2`. -/\n151: def IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n152:     (f : V → Fin 4) : Prop :=\n153:   (∀ v : V, f v = 0 →\n154:       (∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ f u = 3) ∨\n155:       2 ≤ (Finset.univ.filter (fun u => G.Adj v u ∧ f u = 2)).card) ∧\n156:   (∀ v : V, f v = 1 → ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u ∧ 2 ≤ (f u : ℕ))\n157: \n158: /-- Double Roman domination number `γ_dR(G)`. -/\n159: noncomputable def doubleRomanDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V)\n160:     [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n161:   sInf { n | ∃ f : V → Fin 4,\n162:     G.IsDoubleRomanDominatingFunction f ∧ ∑ v, (f v : ℕ) = n }\n163: \n164: -- `radius` is mathlib's (`SimpleGraph.radius : ℕ∞`, the minimum eccentricity);\n165: -- the exporter reads it as `(G.radius).toNat`. On a disconnected graph it is\n166: -- `⊤`, and `.toNat` sends that to `0` — which is precisely why the computable\n167: -- mirror carries `HasRadius` and the exporters emit it as a hypothesis.\n168: \n169: /- ── Graph-class predicates (hypotheses for conditioned conjectures) ──────── -/\n170: \n171: /-- `G` is regular (every vertex the same degree). -/\n172: def IsRegularClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n173:   ∃ d, G.IsRegularOfDegree d\n174: /-- `G` is cubic (3-regular). -/\n175: def IsCubicClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n176:   G.IsRegularOfDegree 3\n177: /-- `G` is subcubic (maximum degree ≤ 3). -/\n178: def IsSubcubicClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n179:   G.maxDegree ≤ 3\n180: /-- `G` is triangle-free. -/\n181: def IsTriangleFreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := G.CliqueFree 3\n182: /-- `G` is `K₄`-free. -/\n183: def IsK4FreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := G.CliqueFree 4\n184: /-- `G` is bipartite (2-colourable). -/\n185: def IsBipartiteClass (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := G.Colorable 2\n186: /-- `G` is Eulerian: connected, with every vertex of even degree.\n187: \n188: Connectivity is part of the definition, not an extra: graphcalc's `eulerian`\n189: column is `networkx.is_eulerian`, which requires a closed Eulerian trail to\n190: exist and so rejects a disconnected graph even when all its degrees are even.\n191: Dropping it here would make this predicate strictly weaker than the hypothesis\n192: the pipeline validated, so a theorem proved against it would not be the\n193: conjecture. Caught by tools/lean_differential.py on the triangle-plus-isolated\n194: -vertex graph, whose degrees are 0, 2, 2, 2. -/\n195: def IsEulerianClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n196:   G.Connected ∧ ∀ v, Even (G.degree v)\n197: /-- `G` is nontrivial (at least two vertices): the graphcalc `nontrivial`\n198: flag, `|V(G)| ≥ 2`, i.e. `2 ≤ G.order`. -/\n199: def IsNontrivialClass (G : SimpleGraph V) : Prop := 2 ≤ G.order\n200: /-- `G` is connected. -/\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
